    description: "ADR-0023 §6 Phase 3 (Unify producers, ~3-5 days estimated by the ADR). Sweep the ~20-30 analyzer sites that emit deprecation-list edge types and rename them to the canonical relationship type, lifting any specialization-carrying fact into edge.meta. Each migration shrinks the property-test offender set; the phase is complete when every endpoint_shape value in the canonical registry has zero production emit sites.\n\nCONTEXT (for a dev picking this up cold):\n\nADR-0023 (docs/adr/0023-edge-type-relationship-not-endpoints.md, currently Draft) classifies edge_type values on the relationship / endpoint_shape / pending_classification axis. PR #3459 landed the canonical registry; PR #3462 added the pre-commit drift linter; PR #3464 added four missing endpoint_shape values plus one reclassification (query_references). PR #3468 (ADR-0024) extracted the abstract axis-declaration template.\n\nPhase 3 is the producer-side rename. It assumes Phase 2 (sibling: WI-sahab-fatoz-zosaj-nopuk-nozon-dosud-mogal-juhim) has migrated consumers to (edge_type, dst.kind) queries that accept BOTH the deprecated specialized edge_type AND the canonical relationship type, so producers can be renamed without breaking consumers mid-flight. Phase 2 must land first.\n\nTHE MIGRATION SHAPE (per ADR-0023 §6 Phase 3):\n\nFor each producer site:\n\n1. Replace the specialized edge_type with the canonical relationship type. Per ADR-0023 §6's deprecation table:\n   - imports_module → imports (consumers query dst.kind == 'module' / 'file')\n   - imports_component → imports (consumers query dst.kind == 'component')\n   - model_reference → references (consumers query dst.kind == 'model')\n   - type_ref → references (consumers query dst.kind == 'type')\n   - query_references → references (consumers query dst.kind == 'query')\n   - renders_component → references + meta['construct']='jsx' (TBD per ADR-0023; pending case-by-case review)\n   - cgo_bridge / napi_bridge / wasm_bridge / ffi_bridge / bridge_invokes / native_bridge → single canonical bridges_to (or fold into calls) + meta['bridge_kind'] for the mechanism\n   - ipc_calls / ipc_event → canonical calls / event_publishes after IPC family audit + meta for the IPC mechanism\n   - implements_rpc / di_resolves → pending_classification family audits resolve canonical landings\n   - wasm_load → needs review; possibly a new canonical 'loads' value or fold into 'imports'\n\n2. If the specialization carried a fact not on the endpoints (bridge mechanism, RPC framework name, IPC transport, etc.), move that fact into edge.meta with a stable key (the existing meta keys for ADR-0015 dataflow access modes are precedent).\n\n3. Run the drift property test after each migration. The endpoint_shape section of the registry stays POPULATED through Phase 3 (deprecated, not removed) — only Phase 4 actually removes the values. So the in-registry/zero-emit invariant is what we're aiming at, not in-registry/in-use.\n\nKNOWN PRODUCER SITES (from the comprehensive sweep performed at PR #3464 close-out, Apr 2026 — captured in WI-tavas-voror's discussion thread, plus the originally-named ADR-0023 cases):\n\nEndpoint_shape values with known emit sites:\n- imports_module — packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/js_module.py (lines 772, 827)\n- imports_component — vue_component.py, vue.py, svelte.py (4 emit sites total)\n- model_reference — orm.py (1)\n- type_ref — js_ts.py (1)\n- renders_component — react_component.py (1)\n- query_references — database_query.py (1)\n- cgo_bridge (1), ffi_bridge (3), napi_bridge (1), wasm_bridge (1), wasm_load (1), bridge_invokes (1), native_bridge (count merged into bridge family) — bridge linkers and native-FFI sites\n- ipc_calls (1), ipc_event (1) — ipc.py / phoenix_ipc.py\n- implements_rpc (1), di_resolves (1) — pending_classification, not endpoint_shape, included here because per-family audits may move them\n\nPRODUCER MIGRATION ORDER (per ADR-0023 §6 directive):\n\n> Start with the dst-kind leakage cases (lowest risk, purely additive on the consumer side), then bridge / FFI, then the publish / dispatch families after their per-family audits.\n\nConcretely:\n1. dst-kind leakage: imports_module, imports_component, model_reference, type_ref, query_references, renders_component (~10 emit sites total).\n2. Bridge / FFI family: cgo_bridge, ffi_bridge, napi_bridge, wasm_bridge, wasm_load, bridge_invokes, native_bridge (~10-12 emit sites).\n3. IPC family: ipc_calls, ipc_event (~2 emit sites) — after IPC per-family audit.\n4. Publish / dispatch families (event_publishes, dispatches_to, routes_to, etc.) — only after their respective per-family audits.\n\nDEPENDENCIES:\n- HARD: Phase 2 (WI-sahab-fatoz) must land first.\n- HARD: per-family audits for dispatch (dispatches_to, routes_to, delegates_to, message_dispatch, annotated_dispatches), publish (event_publishes, event_subscribes, crdt_publishes, annotated_publishes), and IPC (ipc_calls, ipc_event) families — Phase 3's family-touching subset cannot land until these audits pick canonical names. Each audit is a separate sibling tracker item.\n- SOFT: ADR-0023 advancement from Draft to Proposed/Accepted — the §6 specifics for renders_component, the RPC families, and IPC mechanism naming should be settled before producer code is touched.\n\nACCEPTANCE:\n- Every endpoint_shape value in the canonical registry has zero production emit sites (the property test confirms — registry still lists them, no analyzer emits them).\n- Every specialization-carrying fact previously encoded in the edge_type label is preserved either in edge.meta with a documented key OR queryable from src/dst kind.\n- The drift linter still passes; the by-axis view (docs/concept-axes.md) regenerates without changes (the section memberships don't change in Phase 3 — only Phase 4 removes values).\n- Bakeoff validation: tag the merging PR(s) with awaits_bakeoff_validation per AGENTS.md §Bakeoff Validation Discipline so a later DEEP-cycle confirms no slice / ranking / sketch regressions.\n\nSIBLINGS:\n- WI-sahab-fatoz-zosaj-nopuk-nozon-dosud-mogal-juhim — ADR-0023 §6 Phase 2 (must land first).\n- ADR-0023 §6 Phase 4 (Schema bump + deprecation removal) — depends on Phase 3 completion.\n- Per-family audit items for dispatch, publish, IPC families — separate items; Phase 3's family-touching subset waits on each.\n- ADR-0023 advancement from Draft — separate item.\n- WI-tavas-voror-rakiv-litog-gatad-zonoz-holah-tugil (45 emitted-but-unregistered values) — Phase 3 may surface NEW emit sites the original sweep missed; coordinate so neither item rediscovers the other's findings.\n\nBACKGROUND: surfaced as loose-end #4 in the audit-lifecycle session (Apr 2026). ADR-0023's migration plan named Phase 3 in the ADR text but the implementation never started; tracker captures the work so it doesn't slip."  # e6a4
